    {
      "wanneer": "2026-10-23T18:21:50+00:00",
      "gebeurtenis": "taal_na_skrywer",
      "punte": [
        "fix: [taal] in 'Verder af haal mense en diere water uit': 'Haal' does not fit animals, and 'verder af' is loose for downstream.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Was met seep in 'n bak en nie in die rivier self nie.': 'Was' has no object, so it is unclear whether the learner washes themselves, clothes or dishes; correcting it needs the intended content.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Hou 'n toilet ver van 'n boorgat of 'n stroom waar mense water haal.': 'Hou 'n toilet ver' reads oddly, since a toilet cannot be moved; it probably means a toilet should be built or placed far away, but changing the verb would mean guessing the intent.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Die toilet spoel met water en mielies in die land groei daarmee.': 'Groei daarmee' is a slightly wooden way to say crops need water to grow; left unchanged because a smoother version would rephrase the claim."
      ]
    },
